hi I'm Evan Carmichael welcome to  another edition of ask Evan today we're  gonna answer a question from Gerald with  one of my newsletter readers who was  asking about raising capital and  protecting your idea so Gerald wrote  insane I'm trying to bring a travel  product to market and that has a  potential to revolutionize the uber  sighted industry I'm already in  possession of a design patent my issue  is capital is a nondisclosure agreement  form the best way to protect my product  as I discuss my idea with potential  investors so thanks for the question  gerald from my background in bed the  venture capital industry hopefully  there's a few ideas I can share with you  to start off most VCS will not sign in  on the school trip agreement simply  because they're there seen so many  opportunities on a daily basis and so  many products and ideas are so similar  to each other that they would never sign  a nondisclosure agreement so that's  that's kind of step one you can have one  ready and you can ask them to sign it  but for the most part they're gonna say  no really what they're looking for is to  see if you have the plan in place or the  execute so a lot of people have great  ideas but they don't necessarily have  the the plan and the team in place be  able to follow through and turn that  idea into a real business in the venture  capitalists point of view they're being  pitched all the time with all sorts of  ideas and a lot of them are very similar  and 99% of them get rejected and then  once that make it through are the ones  that a have some momentum behind them so  it's not just an idea but you are able  to show that you have either customers  or media's talking about you you build  some kind of momentum up to separate  yourself from everybody else who's  pitching the same idea and also they  look at your team so you know  have has anybody done this before is it  just you or do you have people around  you who've who've been successful as  entrepreneurs who have built something  similar and have since I've had some  success doing it if you don't have  anybody on your team you can go look for  somebody on your team or you can also  build a board of advisers and it's a  loose affiliation with your company it's  not as strict as having a board of  directors but the people who are giving  you advice on how to grow your business  and if they'll lend their name to your  company it can help establish your  credibility with you when you go talk to  investors so you know angels might sign  it but if you look into a venture  capitalist point of view they're not  going to look at signing a nondisclosure  agreement your best bet really is time  to market so it's really only a matter  of time before somebody else goes and  runs with your idea so you want to get  it out there and start talking to  investors and try to get the money you  need to launch your business it doesn't  mean you go and post it all over every  internet forum and that's you know  broadcast exactly what you're doing but  you have to be a little bit more open  when you're talking to investors because  they've seen so many of these ideas and  they're like I'm not going to want to  talk to you if it means they have to  sign it on the scholarship really so  hopefully that helps drill for those of  you watching if you liked the video  please give it a thumbs up below it  makes me want to do more of these videos  for you guys and if you have a question  about what you know Gerald's question is  something similar or you have another  question about your business feel free  to leave it in the comments below I  always read those and try to respond to  as many as I can so thank you and I'll  see you on the next episode  you
 

